# Two products, two maps

QuoteSense has two working products. Pick the pair that matches the task.
Do not use the other product's files to justify edits.

| Task | Plan (how it works) | Action (do not reverse) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Comparison matrix, spaces, packages, GST, PDFs, comparison narrative | [PLAN.md](PLAN.md) then the owning `backend/docs/plan/0N-*.md` or `frontend/docs/plan/0N-*.md` | [ACTION.md](ACTION.md) — never reverse §1–4 |
| Vendor market-rate list/suggest, `pricing_id`, `/by-category`, base-rate banner | [PLAN_RECOMMENDATIONS.md](PLAN_RECOMMENDATIONS.md) | [ACTION_RECOMMENDATIONS.md](ACTION_RECOMMENDATIONS.md) — never reverse §1–4 |

`backend/docs/plan/06-recommend.md` is comparison S6 (matrix narrative).
It is not vendor base rates.

If the request would change a flow that already matches the matching ACTION
file, **do not edit that code**. Explain that it is locked and only change a
stage that is actually broken.

Do **not** run graphify, query a knowledge graph, or write `graphify-out/`.

After changing **comparison** code, update the matching plan file in the same
change:

- new or renamed field → `backend/docs/plan/00-contracts.md` (and the frontend
  mirror if the UI reads it)
- behaviour → that stage's `backend/docs/plan/0N-*.md` or
  `frontend/docs/plan/0N-*.md`
- customer-visible rule → `ACTION.md` (append only; never rewrite §1–4)

After changing **recommendation** code, update in the same change:

- behaviour / fields → `PLAN_RECOMMENDATIONS.md`
- customer-visible rule → `ACTION_RECOMMENDATIONS.md` (append only; never
  rewrite §1–4)

Orient with the plan docs, then Read/Grep the modules they name.
